# Global git excludes.
#
# Git reads this automatically: core.excludesFile defaults to
# $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git/ignore, i.e. ~/.config/git/ignore. This repo clones to
# ~/.config, so the tracked file lands exactly where git looks. That is why
# git/config no longer sets a machine-specific core.excludesFile pointing at
# ~/.gitignore_global.
#
# NOTE: patterns in a repository's own .gitignore override this file. The
# dotfiles repo mirrors the entries below in its .gitignore, because its
# `!dir/**` negations would otherwise resurrect them.

# ---- Editor / OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
*~
.DS_Store

# ---- Agent instruction files stay local to each machine --------------------
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.ignore/
AGENTS.MD

